ve Open Search Information Quick Links. Resources for Current Students Parents and Families Alumni Veterans Community Adjunct Instructor - Undergraduate Nursing (General Call) Home / Employment / Adjunct Instructor – Undergraduate Nursing (General Call) Description of Job Edgewood University is seeking Adjunct Nursing Instructors to join our undergraduate nursing programs. Rooted in the Dominican tradition, Edgewood University is committed to excellence in teaching and learning, with a strong emphasis on ethical leadership, community service, and fostering inclusive, student-centered education. We are currently looking for individuals with expertise as lecturers or clinical instructors in one or more of the following areas: Medical-Surgical Nursing Maternal-Child Health Psychosocial/Behavioral Health Public Health Adult Health Perinatal & Pediatric Nursing Pharmacology Leadership & Healthcare Organizations Evidence-Based Practice Responsibilities Teaching undergraduate nursing students in clinical or classroom settings. Providing timely and constructive feedback. Collaborating with course leads, full-time faculty, and department chairs to support student learning and course delivery. Maintaining a supportive, inclusive, and professional learning environment. Job Qualifications Necessary Education or Work Experience Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) or current enrollment in an MSN program. Unencumbered Wisconsin RN license (or eligibility for licensure). At least two years of full-time (or equivalent) direct patient care experience. Previous teaching experience in an academic or professional setting preferred. Experience in curriculum development and teaching methodologies preferred. Strong multicultural competence and commitment to fostering an inclusive learning environment preferred. Other Qualifications Edgewood University, a Catholic university sponsored by the Dominican Sisters of Sinsinawa, is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to academic excellence through diversity in its faculty, staff, and students. Candidates must demonstrate multicultural competence – the awareness, knowledge, and skills needed to work with others who are culturally different from self in meaningful, relevant, and productive ways. Applicants from traditionally underrepresented populations including women and racial and ethnic minorities are especially encouraged to apply. The selected candidate must actively support the mission of the University by working with faculty, staff and students to share in our core values – truth, compassion, justice, partnership, and community. Must be authorized to work lawfully in the United States without Employer Sponsorship How to Apply Send one PDF document which includes cover letter, resume, and references with a subject line that includes the position code CLSN : Edgewood University Human Resources – CLSN 1000 Edgewood College Drive Madison, WI 53711 E-mail: humanresources@edgewood.edu Equal Opportunity Employer Return to All Job Openings 1000 Edgewood College Dr, Madison, WI 53711 Contact Us About Academics Tuition & Financial Aid Student Life Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Edgewood News Store Employment Directory Resources for: Current Students Parents and Families Edgewood Alumni Veterans Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube © 2026 Edgewood University. All rights reserved. Federal Compliance Non-Discriminatory Policy Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://www.edgewood.edu/employment/associate-professor-of-nursing/": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing - Edgewood University Skip to content Menu Search Search Search Button About More About About Accreditation Leadership Board of Trustees Maps & Directions History Fast Facts Mission, Values, and Inclusion Events This is Edgewood Fast Facts Explore quick facts about our college, academics, student body, and more. View Fast Facts Events Check out what's happening on campus, including fine arts, theatre, music, alumni events, and all student events. See All Events Academics More Academics Academics Academic Calendar Online Learning Institutional Review Board Academic Catalog Academic Support Global Education Honors Program Library Partner Schools Pre-Health Professional Pathways Academic Colleges Programs Discover our 80+ undergraduate and graduate academic programs. Explore All Programs Request a Transcript Request an official copy of your academic records. Request Your Transcript Admissions More Admissions Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Transfer Student Admissions International Undergraduate Admissions Military and Veterans Admissions How to Apply View admissions requirements and get ready to apply to Edgewood University View How to Apply Tuition & Financial Aid More Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Payment Options Scholarships Looking for aid that you don't need to pay back? Check out our scholarships. Jump to Scholarships Student Life More Student Life Student Life Housing Dining Orientation Wellness Center Title IX Disability and Accessibility Services Career Development Cutting Edge Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Campus Ministry Living in Madison Housing Come see where you'll live, learn and make friends on campus. Explore Housing Parking and Safety Get an escort, ride the shuttle service, report a security or safety concern, or get a parking permit. Access Services Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Open Search Information Quick Links. Resources for Current Students Parents and Families Alumni Veterans Community Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing Home / Employment / Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing Description of Job The Henry Predolin School of Nursing at Edgewood University is seeking a full-time, tenure track faculty member for the 2025-26 academic year. The School of Nursing fosters excellence in classroom and clinical settings in both undergraduate and graduate programs. The undergraduate program includes both a traditional and a post-baccalaureate program. Our Master’s (MSN) program has concentration areas in nursing education and nursing administration. A Doctor of Nursing Practice in Leadership (DNP) program is offered both fully online and in a blended format. Join a talented team of nursing professionals by teaching small classes, with a 7:1 student/teacher ratio. Utilize our state-of-the-art clinical simulation lab at the Center for Healthcare Education and Simulation, which features a realistic patient setting that includes patient simulators with high-fidelity mannequins and three real-life, fully equipped patient rooms, each viewable from a control room with one-way glass and closed-circuit monitors and in-lab cameras. Enjoy living in Madison, a vibrant capital city nestled between lakes Mendota and Monona.  Located on the wooded shores of Lake Wingra, Edgewood University is located in a friendly residential community, on a safe and scenic 55-acre campus. It is within walking distance of shopping, restaurants, and recreational and cultural opportunities. Edgewood University is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. The School of Nursing is accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education . Responsibilities Expertise and experience in health care coordination and service delivery. Work collaboratively with Deans and Director(s) in the pre and post licensure nursing programs to teach, develop, implement, refine, revise, and/or evaluate nursing student curriculum and policies. Maintain scholarship and service activities appropriate for rank. Promotes mission, vision, values, and strategic goals of Edgewood University and the Henry Predolin College of Health Sciences. Manages classes and learning environments, selects appropriate materials to support curriculum and provides constructive feedback to students. Delivers effective instruction using technology and a variety of techniques in a manner appropriate to the course objectives. Assesses student learning, designs assessments that measure student growth, aligns assessment with learning opportunities. Promotes continual improvement as part of the cycle of teaching and learning develops and revises curriculum and instructional materials as needed. Participate in processes related to recruitment, selection, admission, advising, and progression of students consistent with the School of Nursing and Edgewood University admission policies, option assessment, and accreditation processes. Pursues professional development and contributes to academic discipline through research, presentations, and publications. Participates in program resource development, including simulation and obtaining intramural and extramural program support. Participate in service through appropriate discipline-specific organizations, educational organizations, statewide boards/ committees, or community activities. Serve on Edgewood University and School of Nursing committees as needed and as indicated in School of Nursing bylaws Represent the University and the School of Nursing at professional activities at local, state, national, and international levels. Other duties as assigned by the Director, School of Nursing Associate Dean for the School of Nursing and Health Sciences, or Dean. Job Qualifications Necessary Education or Work Experience Graduate of an accredited nursing associated with a regionally accredited institution of higher education Doctoral/PhD degree appropriate to content area or near degree completion (final semester) Unencumbered license as a registered nurse and/or Advanced Practice Registered Nurse and eligible for licensure in the state of Wisconsin Commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusivity Minimum of five or more years of clinical experience Preferred Work Experience Graduate level teaching experience Distance/online teaching experience Evidence of scholarship and service Other Qualifications Edgewood University, a Catholic university sponsored by the Dominican Sisters of Sinsinawa, is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to academic excellence through diversity in its faculty, staff, and students. Candidates must demonstrate multicultural competence – the awareness, knowledge, and skills needed to work with others who are culturally different from self in meaningful, relevant, and productive ways. Applicants from traditionally underrepresented populations including women and racial and ethnic minorities are especially encouraged to apply. The selected candidate must actively support the mission of the University by working with faculty, staff and students to share in our core values – truth, compassion, justice, partnership, and community. For more information: Henry Predolin School of Nursing Must be authorized to work lawfully in the United States without Employer Sponsorship How to Apply Send one PDF document which includes a letter of intent, curriculum vitae, official transcripts and two letters of reference (upon request), with a subject line that includes the position code ASNS : Edgewood University Human Resources – ASNS 1000 Edgewood College Drive Madison, WI 53711 E-mail: humanresources@edgewood.edu Equal Opportunity Employer Return to All Job Openings 1000 Edgewood College Dr, Madison, WI 53711 Contact Us About Academics Tuition & Financial Aid Student Life Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Edgewood News Store Employment Directory Resources for: Current Students Parents and Families Edgewood Alumni Veterans Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube © 2026 Edgewood University. All rights reserved. Federal Compliance Non-Discriminatory Policy Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://www.edgewood.edu/employment/lecturer-master-of-arts-in-art-therapy-counseling/": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Lecturer - Master of Arts in Art Therapy/Counseling (Part-Time) - Edgewood University Skip to content Menu Search Search Search Button About More About About Accreditation Leadership Board of Trustees Maps & Directions History Fast Facts Mission, Values, and Inclusion Events This is Edgewood Fast Facts Explore quick facts about our college, academics, student body, and more. View Fast Facts Events Check out what's happening on campus, including fine arts, theatre, music, alumni events, and all student events. See All Events Academics More Academics Academics Academic Calendar Online Learning Institutional Review Board Academic Catalog Academic Support Global Education Honors Program Library Partner Schools Pre-Health Professional Pathways Academic Colleges Programs Discover our 80+ undergraduate and graduate academic programs. Explore All Programs Request a Transcript Request an official copy of your academic records. Request Your Transcript Admissions More Admissions Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Transfer Student Admissions International Undergraduate Admissions Military and Veterans Admissions How to Apply View admissions requirements and get ready to apply to Edgewood University View How to Apply Tuition & Financial Aid More Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Payment Options Scholarships Looking for aid that you don't need to pay back? Check out our scholarships. Jump to Scholarships Student Life More Student Life Student Life Housing Dining Orientation Wellness Center Title IX Disability and Accessibility Services Career Development Cutting Edge Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Campus Ministry Living in Madison Housing Come see where you'll live, learn and make friends on campus. Explore Housing Parking and Safety Get an escort, ride the shuttle service, report a security or safety concern, or get a parking permit. Access Services Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Open Search Information Quick Links. Resources for Current Students Parents and Families Alumni Veterans Community Lecturer – Master of Arts in Art Therapy/Counseling (Part-Time) Home / Employment / Lecturer – Master of Arts in Art Therapy/Counseling (Part-Time) DESCRIPTION OF JOB: Edgewood University is seeking part-time Lecturers to teach in the Master of Arts in Art Therapy and Counseling Program and contribute to student professional development, course management, program assessment, accreditation and quality improvement. The teaching load is 12 credit hours over the 12-month appointment. This appointment is not tenure-track but is renewable on an annual basis at the discretion of the institution. Responsibilities: Teach graduate-level courses in the Master of Arts in Art Therapy and Counseling program (online in Canvas) with synchronous and asynchronous content Revise, and deliver course content aligned with program learning outcomes defined in accord with accreditation and licensing standards Provide timely feedback to students in support of professional development. Maintain virtual office hours Maintain and update course syllabi and Canvas course shells to ensure consistency and quality across assigned courses (courses within assigned pillars) Participation in program assessment, data collection, analysis, and reporting. Participate in quality improvement activities including class visits, reviews of instructional practices, and provision of constructive feedback Participation in Students’ Thesis committees Attend and participate in planning for residencies, one virtual (August) and one in-person (April) program faculty meetings JOB QUALIFICATIONS Necessary Education or Work Experience: Doctorate in Art Therapy, Counseling and/or Psychology preferred Registered, Board Certified Art Therapist ATR-BC, Licensed LPC or equivalent, or license eligible in Wisconsin preferred Active participation in state, national, and local professional organizations Evidence of continuing scholarly work and competence in teaching Candidates must have excellent communication skills, flexibility, mature judgment, and a commitment to teaching in a creative, collaborative and values-based environment with a focus on promoting individual student success. Minimum of three years graduate teaching experience. Recent clinical practice; Minimum of at least three years within the past fifteen years Required Knowledge and Skills: Knowledge of the fields of Counseling and Art Therapy WI State standards for licensure Microsoft Word and Excel Excellent oral and written communication skills Effective skills in teaching and mentoring Other Qualifications: Edgewood University, a Catholic university sponsored by the Dominican Sisters of Sinsinawa, is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to academic excellence through diversity in its faculty, staff, and students. Candidates must demonstrate multicultural competence – the awareness, knowledge, and skills needed to work with others who are culturally different from self in meaningful, relevant, and productive ways. Applicants from traditionally underrepresented populations including women and racial and ethnic minorities are especially encouraged to apply. The selected candidate must actively support the mission of the University by working with faculty, staff and students to share in our core values – truth, compassion, justice, partnership, and community. Must be authorized to work lawfully in the United States without Employer Sponsorship. How to Apply Send one PDF document which includes cover letter, resume, and references with a subject line that includes the position code ATHE: Edgewood University Human Resources – ATHE 1000 Edgewood College Drive Madison, WI 53711 E-mail: humanresources@edgewood.edu Equal Opportunity Employer Return to All Job Openings 1000 Edgewood College Dr, Madison, WI 53711 Contact Us About Academics Tuition & Financial Aid Student Life Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Edgewood News Store Employment Directory Resources for: Current Students Parents and Families Edgewood Alumni Veterans Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube © 2026 Edgewood University. All rights reserved. Federal Compliance Non-Discriminatory Policy Privacy Statement"
