Resources for Current Students Parents and Families Alumni Veterans Community Custodial Manager Home / Employment / Custodial Manager DESCRIPTION OF JOB: The Custodial Manager is a working supervisor responsible for daily leadership, scheduling, training, and performance management of custodial staff across all shifts. This role ensures University standards for cleanliness, sanitation, and appearance are consistently met and reports to the Assistant Director of Facilities Operations. The position requires hands-on supervision, strong janitorial expertise, and a commitment to delivering excellent customer service while maintaining a clean, safe, and well-presented campus environment. This role primarily supports second and third shift operations. The typical schedule is Monday through Thursday, approximately 2:30 PM to 11:00 PM. Friday hours are flexible and determined based on operational needs and staff availability. Responsibilities: Management, Supervision & Training Supervise custodial staff and student workers, including scheduling, task assignment, coaching, and performance evaluation. Train employees in proper cleaning techniques, equipment operation, safety protocols, and efficient use of materials. Inspect work regularly and direct corrective actions to ensure cleanliness and safety standards. Maintain accurate personnel and training records. Ensure compliance with safety regulations, EPA standards, and University custodial policies. Report facility hazards or safety risks as needed. Custodial Duties Clean classrooms, offices, meeting rooms, and common areas. Operate various types of cleaning machines, i.e. floor machines, waxers, and polishers. Empty trash, recycling, and refuse containers. Perform snow removal as needed. Support upkeep of parking structures and ensure proper recycling practices. Operational Oversight of Supplies & Equipment Maintain custodial supply levels and reorder materials as needed. Manage inventory of custodial closets and ensure safe chemical storage. Inspect custodial equipment and coordinate repairs or replacement as needed. Additional Duties Oversee the setup of rooms and spaces for university events. Serve on Facilities-related committees as assigned. Assist the Director of Facilities Operations with routine departmental work as requested. Work with the Event Services Manager to prepare residence halls for occupants attending summer programs. JOB QUALIFICATIONS Necessary Education or Work Experience: High School Diploma or equivalent. Minimum of five years supervisory experience; preference for managing 15 or more staff. At least two years of custodial experience. Valid driver’s license. Incumbent must pass a satisfactory motor vehicle check Required Knowledge and Skills: Proficiency in Spanish preferred Knowledge of custodial procedures, chemicals, and equipment. Ability to train staff effectively in cleaning techniques and equipment use. Computer literacy including Word, Excel, and ability to learn new systems. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to conduct group training sessions. Ability to work collaboratively with staff and University partners Other Qualifications: Edgewood University, a Catholic university sponsored by the Dominican Sisters of Sinsinawa, is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to academic excellence through diversity in its faculty, staff, and students. Candidates must demonstrate multicultural competence – the awareness, knowledge, and skills needed to work with others who are culturally different from self in meaningful, relevant, and productive ways. Applicants from traditionally underrepresented populations including women and racial and ethnic minorities are especially encouraged to apply. The selected candidate must actively support the mission of the University by working with faculty, staff and students to share in our core values – truth, compassion, justice, partnership, and community. Must be authorized to work lawfully in the United States without Employer Sponsorship. How to Apply Send one PDF document which includes cover letter, resume, and references with a subject line that includes the position code CMAN : Edgewood University Human Resources – CMA N 1000 Edgewood College Drive Madison, WI 53711 E-mail: humanresources@edgewood.edu Equal Opportunity Employer Return to All Job Openings 1000 Edgewood College Dr, Madison, WI 53711 Contact Us About Academics Tuition & Financial Aid Student Life Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Edgewood News Store Employment Directory Resources for: Current Students Parents and Families Edgewood Alumni Veterans Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube © 2026 Edgewood University. All rights reserved. Federal Compliance Non-Discriminatory Policy Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://www.edgewood.edu/employment/graduate-programs-coordinator-college-of-business-communication-and-technology/": {
      "title": "Graduate Programs Coordinator",
      "description": "Graduate Programs Coordinator - College of Business, Communication, and Technology - Edgewood University Skip to content Menu Search Search Search Button About More About About Accreditation Leadership Board of Trustees Maps & Directions History Fast Facts Mission, Values, and Inclusion Events This is Edgewood Fast Facts Explore quick facts about our college, academics, student body, and more. View Fast Facts Events Check out what's happening on campus, including fine arts, theatre, music, alumni events, and all student events. See All Events Academics More Academics Academics Academic Calendar Online Learning Institutional Review Board Academic Catalog Academic Support Global Education Honors Program Library Partner Schools Pre-Health Professional Pathways Academic Colleges Programs Discover our 80+ undergraduate and graduate academic programs. Explore All Programs Request a Transcript Request an official copy of your academic records. Request Your Transcript Admissions More Admissions Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Transfer Student Admissions International Undergraduate Admissions Military and Veterans Admissions How to Apply View admissions requirements and get ready to apply to Edgewood University View How to Apply Tuition & Financial Aid More Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Payment Options Scholarships Looking for aid that you don't need to pay back? Check out our scholarships. Jump to Scholarships Student Life More Student Life Student Life Housing Dining Orientation Wellness Center Title IX Disability and Accessibility Services Career Development Cutting Edge Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Campus Ministry Living in Madison Housing Come see where you'll live, learn and make friends on campus. Explore Housing Parking and Safety Get an escort, ride the shuttle service, report a security or safety concern, or get a parking permit. Access Services Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Open Search Information Quick Links. Resources for Current Students Parents and Families Alumni Veterans Community Graduate Programs Coordinator – College of Business, Communication, and Technology Home / Employment / Graduate Programs Coordinator – College of Business, Communication, and Technology DESCRIPTION OF JOB: The Graduate Programs Coordinator provides high-level administrative, operational, and student-support leadership within the College of Business, Communication, and Technology. This role serves as the primary liaison between graduate students, faculty, university administration, and outside entities ensuring that academic programs run smoothly and students are supported from enrollment through graduation. Responsibilities: Academic and Administrative Coordination Coordinate day-to-day program operations, ensuring compliance with institutional policies and accreditation standards Oversee course scheduling and ensure adjunct faculty payment occurs. Assist the director in compiling data for reports and enrollment trends. Assist the director in creating systems and processes within the graduate programs to improve the student experience and retention. Assist the director in evaluating, designing, and implementing administrative systems to improve departmental workflow and communication. Assist the director in hiring adjunct faculty both domestically and ROW. Student Success and Advising Coordinate orientation and learning sessions for graduate students to familiarize them with college resources and practices. Coordinate with advising to monitor student academic standing, ensuring degree requirements and milestones are met. Act as the first point of contact for student questions and filter questions to appropriate parties. Required Knowledge and Skills: Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred. Minimum of 3 years of experience in higher education administration or student services. Proficiency with Student Information Systems (SIS) and CRM platforms (e.g., Slate, Banner). Excellent professional communication and the ability to handle sensitive FERPA-regulated data. Other Qualifications: Edgewood University, a Catholic university sponsored by the Dominican Sisters of Sinsinawa, is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to academic excellence through diversity in its faculty, staff, and students. Candidates must demonstrate multicultural competence – the awareness, knowledge, and skills needed to work with others who are culturally different from self in meaningful, relevant, and productive ways. Applicants from traditionally underrepresented populations including women and racial and ethnic minorities are especially encouraged to apply. The selected candidate must actively support the mission of the University by working with faculty, staff and students to share in our core values – truth, compassion, justice, partnership, and community. Must be authorized to work lawfully in the United States without Employer Sponsorship. How to Apply Send one PDF document which includes cover letter, resume, and references with a subject line that includes the position code GRPC : Edgewood University Human Resources – GRPC 1000 Edgewood College Drive Madison, WI 53711 E-mail: humanresources@edgewood.edu Equal Opportunity Employer Return to All Job Openings 1000 Edgewood College Dr, Madison, WI 53711 Contact Us About Academics Tuition & Financial Aid Student Life Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Edgewood News Store Employment Directory Resources for: Current Students Parents and Families Edgewood Alumni Veterans Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube © 2026 Edgewood University. All rights reserved. Federal Compliance Non-Discriminatory Policy Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://www.edgewood.edu/employment/head-mens-volleyball-coach/": {
      "title": "Head Men's Volleyball Coach",
      "description": "Head Men's Volleyball Coach - Edgewood University Skip to content Menu Search Search Search Button About More About About Accreditation Leadership Board of Trustees Maps & Directions History Fast Facts Mission, Values, and Inclusion Events This is Edgewood Fast Facts Explore quick facts about our college, academics, student body, and more. View Fast Facts Events Check out what's happening on campus, including fine arts, theatre, music, alumni events, and all student events. See All Events Academics More Academics Academics Academic Calendar Online Learning Institutional Review Board Academic Catalog Academic Support Global Education Honors Program Library Partner Schools Pre-Health Professional Pathways Academic Colleges Programs Discover our 80+ undergraduate and graduate academic programs. Explore All Programs Request a Transcript Request an official copy of your academic records. Request Your Transcript Admissions More Admissions Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Transfer Student Admissions International Undergraduate Admissions Military and Veterans Admissions How to Apply View admissions requirements and get ready to apply to Edgewood University View How to Apply Tuition & Financial Aid More Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Payment Options Scholarships Looking for aid that you don't need to pay back? Check out our scholarships. Jump to Scholarships Student Life More Student Life Student Life Housing Dining Orientation Wellness Center Title IX Disability and Accessibility Services Career Development Cutting Edge Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Campus Ministry Living in Madison Housing Come see where you'll live, learn and make friends on campus. Explore Housing Parking and Safety Get an escort, ride the shuttle service, report a security or safety concern, or get a parking permit. Access Services Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Open Search Information Quick Links. Resources for Current Students Parents and Families Alumni Veterans Community Head Men’s Volleyball Coach Home / Employment / Head Men’s Volleyball Coach DESCRIPTION OF JOB: The Head Men’s Volleyball Coach is responsible for leading all aspects of Edgewood University’s established NCAA Division III Men’s Volleyball program, including recruiting and retaining qualified student-athletes, coaching, student-athlete development, budget management, alumni and community engagement, and compliance with NCAA, Northern Athletics Collegiate Conference (NACC), and institutional policies. The Head Coach is expected to build upon the program’s existing foundation while fostering a positive, inclusive, and competitive team culture that supports the mission of Edgewood University Athletics and emphasizes academic achievement, personal growth, leadership, and competitive excellence. Athletics plays an important role in the life of the University, including enhancing the learning experience for student-athletes, creating opportunities to unite the campus community, publicly demonstrating the University’s values and mission, and contributing to the achievement of institutional goals. The position is responsible for short- and long-term program planning that supports the University’s Mission and Vision and strictly adheres to NCAA, NACC, and institutional rules and regulations. Responsibilities: Program Leadership and Student-Athlete Development Lead all aspects of the Men’s Volleyball program in a manner consistent with the mission and values of Edgewood University and Edgewood University Athletics while building upon established program standards and traditions. Develop a team culture centered on accountability, respect, teamwork, communication, and competitive excellence. Plan, organize, and conduct productive practice sessions, team meetings, conditioning sessions, and competitions. Teach the technical, tactical, physical, and mental aspects of volleyball, including serving, passing, setting, attacking, blocking, team defense, and situational play. Prepare student-athletes for high levels of NCAA Division III and NACC competition. Support the academic, personal, leadership, and career development of each student-athlete. Model and foster appropriate sportsmanship, competitiveness, humility, and professionalism. Work collaboratively with Athletic Training, Athletic Performance, Academic Success, Division of Student Development, and other campus partners to support student-athlete well-being and success. Develop annual competitive goals and evaluate program progress and success. Recruiting and Enrollment Management Develop and execute a comprehensive recruiting strategy to identify, attract, and enroll academically and athletically qualified student-athletes. Build and maintain relationships with prospective student-athletes, parents and guardians, high school and club coaches, alumni, and other recruiting influencers within regional and national men’s volleyball networks. Partner closely with the Admissions Office throughout the recruiting process. Utilize departmental recruiting software, CRM systems, and appropriate communication tools to manage recruiting activity. Maintain roster numbers consistent with departmental expectations, program needs, and institutional enrollment goals. Recruit and retain student-athletes who contribute positively to the program, department, and University community. Foster retention through an exceptional student-athlete experience. Program Administration Manage the program operating budget, booster budget, and related financial activity in accordance with departmental and institutional policies. Coordinate scheduling, team travel, equipment, apparel, gymnasium and practice needs, and game-day operations in collaboration with Athletics staff. Supervise assistant coaches, graduate assistants, student managers, student assistants, and other team personnel. Complete required administrative responsibilities accurately and in a timely manner. Assist with fundraising, alumni engagement, and program support initiatives in collaboration with Athletics and Advancement. Compliance Oversight Maintain a current working knowledge of NCAA Division III, NACC, and institutional rules and regulations. Ensure the Men’s Volleyball program operates in full compliance with all applicable rules, policies, and procedures. Educate assistant coaches, student-athletes, boosters, alumni, and parents or guardians regarding applicable NCAA, NACC, and institutional expectations. Complete required compliance documentation and reporting in a timely and accurate manner. Promote a culture of integrity and accountability within the program. Community Engagement and Alumni Relations Develop and foster community relationships that benefit the Men’s Volleyball program, Athletics Department, and University. Facilitate team involvement in meaningful community service and campus engagement opportunities. Complete at least one community service project with the Men’s Volleyball team each year and participate in at least one Athletics Department community service project. Expand the program’s supporters, alumni connections, and campus and community visibility. Assist in developing, fostering, and maintaining practice and competition venue relationships. Represent the University and Athletics Department at departmental, institutional, alumni, and community events. Other Duties Attend Athletics Department staff meetings, team and individual meetings, and other institutional meetings as appropriate. Participate in University-wide committees, task forces, and special projects as assigned. Support Athletics Department events, including the annual golf outing, Hall of Fame, Athletics Awards Ceremony, and other departmental initiatives. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Leadership Expectations The Head Men’s Volleyball Coach is expected to: Model the mission and values of Edgewood University Athletics. Create an inclusive environment where student-athletes can thrive academically, athletically, and personally. Collaborate positively with colleagues across the department and campus. Demonstrate professionalism, integrity, accountability, and effective communication. Contribute to a culture of continuous improvement and shared departmental success. Prioritize meaningful relationships, team-oriented experiences, and personal growth for student-athletes. JOB QUALIFICATIONS Necessary Education or Work Experience: Bachelor’s degree required. Collegiate coaching and/or recruiting experience required. Demonstrated ability to recruit, develop, and retain successful student-athletes. Demonstrated commitment to NCAA Division III philosophy and student-athlete development. Preferred Education and Experience Master’s degree preferred. Head coaching and/or collegiate men’s volleyball coaching experience preferred. Experience using recruiting software, CRM systems, and volleyball video analysis platforms preferred. Experience building relationships with high school and club volleyball programs, alumni, and community partners preferred. Required Knowledge and Skills: Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Strong organizational, planning, and relationship-building skills. Working knowledge of NCAA Division III rules and regulations. Ability to relate effectively to a diverse population of students, colleagues, alumni, families, and community members. Understanding of and ability to support the Edgewood University Mission and Values. Valid driver’s license and ability to meet institutional driving requirements. Specialized Technology Skills: Comfortable with Microsoft Office 365 platform. Comfortable using recruiting CRM systems, such as Slate or equivalent platforms. Comfortable using volleyball video analysis and scouting software, such as HUDL, VolleyMetrics, or equivalent platforms. Demonstrated ability to use social media platforms appropriately and effectively for program communication and promotion. Other Qualifications: Edgewood University, a Catholic university sponsored by the Dominican Sisters of Sinsinawa, is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to academic excellence through diversity in its faculty, staff, and students. Candidates must demonstrate multicultural competence – the awareness, knowledge, and skills needed to work with others who are culturally different from self in meaningful, relevant, and productive ways. Applicants from traditionally underrepresented populations including women and racial and ethnic minorities are especially encouraged to apply. The selected candidate must actively support the mission of the University by working with faculty, staff and students to share in our core values – truth, compassion, justice, partnership, and community. Must be authorized to work lawfully in the United States without Employer Sponsorship. How to Apply Send one PDF document which includes cover letter, resume, and references with a subject line that includes the position code HVBC : Edgewood University Human Resources – HVBC 1000 Edgewood College Drive Madison, WI 53711 E-mail: humanresources@edgewood.edu Equal Opportunity Employer Return to All Job Openings 1000 Edgewood College Dr, Madison, WI 53711 Contact Us About Academics Tuition & Financial Aid Student Life Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Edgewood News Store Employment Directory Resources for: Current Students Parents and Families Edgewood Alumni Veterans Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube © 2026 Edgewood University. All rights reserved. Federal Compliance Non-Discriminatory Policy Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://www.edgewood.edu/employment/head-womens-flag-football-coach/": {
      "title": "Head Women's Flag Football Coach",
      "description": "Head Women's Flag Football Coach - Edgewood University Skip to content Menu Search Search Search Button About More About About Accreditation Leadership Board of Trustees Maps & Directions History Fast Facts Mission, Values, and Inclusion Events This is Edgewood Fast Facts Explore quick facts about our college, academics, student body, and more. View Fast Facts Events Check out what's happening on campus, including fine arts, theatre, music, alumni events, and all student events. See All Events Academics More Academics Academics Academic Calendar Online Learning Institutional Review Board Academic Catalog Academic Support Global Education Honors Program Library Partner Schools Pre-Health Professional Pathways Academic Colleges Programs Discover our 80+ undergraduate and graduate academic programs. Explore All Programs Request a Transcript Request an official copy of your academic records. Request Your Transcript Admissions More Admissions Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Transfer Student Admissions International Undergraduate Admissions Military and Veterans Admissions How to Apply View admissions requirements and get ready to apply to Edgewood University View How to Apply Tuition & Financial Aid More Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Payment Options Scholarships Looking for aid that you don't need to pay back? Check out our scholarships. Jump to Scholarships Student Life More Student Life Student Life Housing Dining Orientation Wellness Center Title IX Disability and Accessibility Services Career Development Cutting Edge Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Campus Ministry Living in Madison Housing Come see where you'll live, learn and make friends on campus. Explore Housing Parking and Safety Get an escort, ride the shuttle service, report a security or safety concern, or get a parking permit. Access Services Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Open Search Information Quick Links. Resources for Current Students Parents and Families Alumni Veterans Community Head Women’s Flag Football Coach Home / Employment / Head Women’s Flag Football Coach DESCRIPTION OF JOB: The Head Women’s Flag Football Coach is responsible for launching and leading all aspects of the University’s new NCAA Division III Women’s Flag Football program. Responsibilities include establishing the program’s competitive and cultural foundation; recruiting and retaining qualified student-athletes; coaching and student-athlete development; scheduling; budget and equipment management; external partnerships; and compliance with NCAA, applicable conference or league, and institutional policies. As the inaugural head coach, this position will build the program’s identity, roster, operating practices, and long-term strategy while fostering a positive, inclusive, and competitive team culture that emphasizes academic achievement, personal growth, leadership, and competitive excellence. Athletics plays an important role in the life of the University, including enhancing the learning experience for student-athletes, creating opportunities to unite the campus community, publicly demonstrating the University’s values and mission, and contributing to the achievement of institutional goals. The position is responsible for short- and long-term program planning that supports the University’s Mission and Vision and strictly adheres to NCAA, applicable conference or league, and institutional rules and regulations. Responsibilities: Program Launch, Leadership, and Student-Athlete Development Launch and lead the Women’s Flag Football program in a manner consistent with the mission and values of Edgewood University and Edgewood University Athletics. Develop and execute a comprehensive launch plan that establishes the program’s identity, culture, operating standards, competitive goals, and path toward sustainable success. Build a team culture centered on accountability, respect, teamwork, communication, inclusion, and competitive excellence. Plan, organize, and conduct productive practice sessions, team meetings, conditioning sessions, and competitions. Teach the technical, tactical, physical, and mental aspects of flag football, including offensive and defensive concepts, position-specific skills, safe technique, and situational decision-making. Support the academic, personal, leadership, and career development of each student-athlete. Model and foster appropriate sportsmanship, competitiveness, humility, integrity, and professionalism. Work collaboratively with Athletic Training, Athletic Performance, Academic Success, Division of Student Development, and other campus partners to support student-athlete well-being and success. Establish annual launch and competitive benchmarks, evaluate program progress, and adjust strategies as the sport and collegiate landscape evolve. Recruiting and Enrollment Management Develop and execute a comprehensive recruiting strategy to identify, attract, and enroll academically and athletically qualified student-athletes for the inaugural roster and future classes. Build relationships with prospective student-athletes, families, high school and club coaches, state associations, and other recruiting influencers within the expanding girls’ flag football ecosystem, including NFL FLAG and multi-sport pathways. Partner closely with the Admissions Office throughout the recruiting process. Utilize departmental recruiting software, CRM systems, video evaluation, and appropriate communication tools to manage recruiting activity. Build and maintain a competitive roster consistent with departmental expectations, program needs, and institutional enrollment goals, with an anticipated roster range of approximately 18 to 25 student-athletes. Recruit and retain student-athletes who contribute positively to the program, department, and University community. Foster retention through an exceptional student-athlete experience. Program Administration Manage the program operating budget, booster budget, and related financial activity in accordance with departmental and institutional policies. Develop a competitive spring schedule that meets current NCAA sport sponsorship and minimum contest requirements, and coordinate team travel, facilities, game-day operations, officials, and sport-specific field setup. Coordinate the purchasing, inventory, maintenance, and replacement of uniforms, footballs, flag belts, mouthguards, field markers, and other program equipment. Supervise assistant coaches, graduate assistants, student managers, student assistants, and other team personnel, as applicable, and complete required administrative responsibilities accurately and on time. Assist with fundraising, grant opportunities, alumni engagement, and program support initiatives in collaboration with Athletics and Advancement. Compliance Oversight Maintain a current working knowledge of NCAA Division III, Emerging Sports for Women, applicable conference or league, and institutional rules and regulations. Ensure the Women’s Flag Football program operates in full compliance with all applicable rules, policies, procedures, playing rules, and sport sponsorship requirements. Ensure student-athletes complete required eligibility certification processes and maintain accurate compliance, roster, sport sponsorship, and competition records. Educate assistant coaches, student-athletes, boosters, alumni, and parents or guardians regarding applicable NCAA, conference or league, and institutional expectations. Promote a culture of integrity and accountability within the program. Community Engagement, Visibility, and External Partnerships Develop relationships with high school associations, youth and club organizations, USA Football, RCX Sports Foundation, NFL FLAG, local professional football partners, and other organizations that benefit the program and University. Create clinics, camps, showcases, and other engagement opportunities that expand access to the sport and strengthen the program’s recruiting pipeline and community visibility. Facilitate meaningful campus engagement and complete at least one team community service project each year, in addition to participating in at least one Athletics Department service project. Build the program’s base of supporters and develop alumni engagement traditions as the program grows. Represent the University and Athletics Department at departmental, institutional, recruiting, partner, alumni, and community events. Other Duties Attend Athletics Department staff meetings, team and individual meetings, and other institutional meetings as appropriate. Participate in University-wide committees, task forces, and special projects as assigned. Support Athletics Department events, including the annual golf outing, Hall of Fame, Athletics Awards Ceremony, and other departmental initiatives. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Leadership Expectations The Head Women’s Flag Football Coach is expected to: Model the mission and values of Edgewood University Athletics. Serve as an entrepreneurial program builder who can translate a vision into clear priorities, systems, and measurable progress. Create an inclusive environment where student-athletes can thrive academically, athletically, and personally. Collaborate positively with colleagues across the department and campus. Demonstrate professionalism, integrity, accountability, adaptability, and effective communication. Contribute to continuous improvement and shared departmental success while prioritizing meaningful relationships, team-oriented experiences, and personal growth for student-athletes. JOB QUALIFICATIONS Necessary Education or Work Experience: Bachelor’s degree required. Coaching and/or recruiting experience at the collegiate, high school, club, or elite youth level, with demonstrated knowledge of flag football or football rules, strategies, skill development, and safe coaching practices. Demonstrated ability to recruit, develop, and retain successful student-athletes and to organize and lead a new initiative, program, or team. Demonstrated commitment to NCAA Division III philosophy and holistic student-athlete development. Preferred Education and Experience Master’s degree preferred. Head coaching, coordinator, or comparable program leadership experience preferred. Experience coaching women’s or girls’ flag football and/or launching or significantly growing a team, program, or sport offering preferred. Collegiate coaching and recruiting experience preferred. Established flag football recruiting relationships and relevant coaching certification through USA Football or a comparable organization preferred. Experience using recruiting software, CRM systems, and video analysis platforms preferred. Required Knowledge and Skills: Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Strong organizational, planning, project management, and relationship-building skills. Ability to build systems and solve problems in a new-program environment. Working knowledge of NCAA Division III rules and regulations, or the demonstrated ability to acquire that knowledge quickly. Ability to relate effectively to a diverse population of students, colleagues, alumni, families, and community members. Understanding of and ability to support the Edgewood University Mission and Values. Valid driver’s license and ability to meet institutional driving requirements. Specialized Technology Skills: Comfortable with Microsoft Office 365 platform. Comfortable using recruiting CRM systems, such as Slate or equivalent platforms. Comfortable using video analysis and scouting software, such as HUDL or equivalent platforms. Demonstrated ability to use social media platforms appropriately and effectively for program communication, recruiting, and promotion. Other Qualifications: Edgewood University, a Catholic university sponsored by the Dominican Sisters of Sinsinawa, is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to academic excellence through diversity in its faculty, staff, and students. Candidates must demonstrate multicultural competence – the awareness, knowledge, and skills needed to work with others who are culturally different from self in meaningful, relevant, and productive ways. Applicants from traditionally underrepresented populations including women and racial and ethnic minorities are especially encouraged to apply. The selected candidate must actively support the mission of the University by working with faculty, staff and students to share in our core values – truth, compassion, justice, partnership, and community. Must be authorized to work lawfully in the United States without Employer Sponsorship. How to Apply Send one PDF document which includes cover letter, resume, and references with a subject line that includes the position code HWFF : Edgewood University Human Resources – HWFF 1000 Edgewood College Drive Madison, WI 53711 E-mail: humanresources@edgewood.edu Equal Opportunity Employer Return to All Job Openings 1000 Edgewood College Dr, Madison, WI 53711 Contact Us About Academics Tuition & Financial Aid Student Life Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Edgewood News Store Employment Directory Resources for: Current Students Parents and Families Edgewood Alumni Veterans Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube © 2026 Edgewood University. All rights reserved. Federal Compliance Non-Discriminatory Policy Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://www.edgewood.edu/employment/maintenance-technician-electrical/": {
      "title": "Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Maintenance Technician - Electrical - Edgewood University Skip to content Menu Search Search Search Button About More About About Accreditation Leadership Board of Trustees Maps & Directions History Fast Facts Mission, Values, and Inclusion Events This is Edgewood Fast Facts Explore quick facts about our college, academics, student body, and more. View Fast Facts Events Check out what's happening on campus, including fine arts, theatre, music, alumni events, and all student events. See All Events Academics More Academics Academics Academic Calendar Online Learning Institutional Review Board Academic Catalog Academic Support Global Education Honors Program Library Partner Schools Pre-Health Professional Pathways Academic Colleges Programs Discover our 80+ undergraduate and graduate academic programs. Explore All Programs Request a Transcript Request an official copy of your academic records. Request Your Transcript Admissions More Admissions Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Transfer Student Admissions International Undergraduate Admissions Military and Veterans Admissions How to Apply View admissions requirements and get ready to apply to Edgewood University View How to Apply Tuition & Financial Aid More Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Payment Options Scholarships Looking for aid that you don't need to pay back? Check out our scholarships. Jump to Scholarships Student Life More Student Life Student Life Housing Dining Orientation Wellness Center Title IX Disability and Accessibility Services Career Development Cutting Edge Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Campus Ministry Living in Madison Housing Come see where you'll live, learn and make friends on campus. Explore Housing Parking and Safety Get an escort, ride the shuttle service, report a security or safety concern, or get a parking permit. Access Services Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Open Search Information Quick Links. Resources for Current Students Parents and Families Alumni Veterans Community Maintenance Technician – Electrical Home / Employment / Maintenance Technician – Electrical DESCRIPTION OF JOB: Primary responsibilities include the maintenance, repair, troubleshooting, and improvement of campus electrical and lighting systems. The position is designed for a skilled technician who can work both independently and as a member of the Facilities Operations team to improve the maintenance, reliability, safety, and energy efficiency of campus facilities. The Maintenance Technician – Electrical is responsible for maintaining campus electrical and lighting systems, including the replacement of lamps, ballasts, fixtures, controls, and related equipment. Strong customer service skills are essential. Successful candidates will demonstrate a strong work ethic, positive attitude, initiative, and a commitment to continuous improvement within the Facilities Operations Department. Responsibilities: Maintain and Repair Campus Electrical and Lighting Systems Maintain recommended and appropriate interior and exterior light levels following IES guidelines using appropriate lamps, ballasts, fixtures, and controls. Perform preventive maintenance on campus lighting systems including cleaning and maintaining lamps, ballasts, fixtures, lenses, louvers, and reflective surfaces. Troubleshoot and repair lighting and electrical system issues. Replace ballasts, lamps, fixtures, switches, outlets, and other electrical components as necessary. Identify electrical maintenance needs and report situations requiring specialized contractor services to the Director of Facilities Operations. Assist with planning and implementation of lighting upgrades and replacement projects that improve energy efficiency. Assist with campus re-lamping projects and lighting replacement schedules. Perform maintenance and testing of fire alarm control panels, smoke detectors, and carbon monoxide detection systems as assigned. Enter and complete work orders accurately and in a timely manner using the computerized work order management system. Maintain records of maintenance activities and repairs. Utilize the AkitaBox work order system effectively. Support Facility Maintenance Planning and Asset Management Collect building condition information and report deficiencies, hazards, deterioration, and equipment concerns to the Director of Facilities Operations. Assist in maintaining equipment inventories and asset records. Identify maintenance and replacement needs related to electrical systems and campus infrastructure. Provide recommendations regarding lifecycle replacement of electrical equipment and lighting systems. Assist in documenting maintenance activities and equipment conditions for future planning purposes. Assist the Director of Facilities Operations with coordinating and monitoring the work of electrical contractors to ensure projects are completed in accordance with specifications, safety requirements, and College standards. Assist the Director of Facilities Operations in obtaining quotes and bids for electrical repairs, equipment replacement, and capital improvement projects. Provide technical information and recommendations to support contractor selection, project planning, and scope development for electrical work. Support Energy Efficiency and Sustainability Initiatives Assist with implementation of energy conservation and sustainability projects. Participate in meetings and activities associated with energy efficiency initiatives. Assist in identifying opportunities to improve energy performance through lighting upgrades, controls, and operational improvements. Support evaluation of HVAC and energy-related equipment performance as needed. Help gather information required for utility incentive and rebate programs. Perform General Maintenance Duties This may include one or more of the following areas depending upon skills and expertise: Appliance maintenance and repair. Painting and drywall repairs. Basic plumbing repairs. Carpentry work. Locksmith and key work. Structural repairs. Roofing repairs. Small motor repair. HVAC maintenance support. Elevator maintenance coordination. Follow all University policies, department procedures, and safety regulations. Perform other routine Facilities Operations work as assigned by the Director of Facilities Operations. Provide support to other maintenance staff and participate in on-call rotations as needed. JOB QUALIFICATIONS Necessary Education or Work Experience: Successful completion of a trade school electrical program or a minimum of five years of experience in electrical and lighting maintenance and repair preferred. Journeyman Electrician license preferred. Experience with commercial or institutional building electrical systems preferred. Valid driver’s license and successful University MVR check required. Required Knowledge and Skills: Working knowledge of building electrical systems. Working knowledge of lamps, ballasts, sensors, controls, and fixtures. Ability to troubleshoot and repair electrical and lighting systems. Knowledge of electrical safety practices and applicable codes. Computer literacy including proficiency with Microsoft Excel and Word and the ability to learn new software applications. Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Ability to provide excellent customer service. Ability to meet the public professionally and work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students. Walking, bending, climbing, and lifting may be required. Attend meetings, seminars, and workshops as required. Ability to be on call for urgent or emergency situations on a rotating basis. Spanish proficiency is a plus. Other Qualifications: Edgewood University, a Catholic university sponsored by the Dominican Sisters of Sinsinawa, is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to academic excellence through diversity in its faculty, staff, and students. Candidates must demonstrate multicultural competence – the awareness, knowledge, and skills needed to work with others who are culturally different from self in meaningful, relevant, and productive ways. Applicants from traditionally underrepresented populations including women and racial and ethnic minorities are especially encouraged to apply. The selected candidate must actively support the mission of the University by working with faculty, staff and students to share in our core values – truth, compassion, justice, partnership, and community. Must be authorized to work lawfully in the United States without Employer Sponsorship. How to Apply Send one PDF document which includes cover letter, resume, and references with a subject line that includes the position code MLEC : Edgewood University Human Resources – MELC 1000 Edgewood College Drive Madison, WI 53711 E-mail: humanresources@edgewood.edu Equal Opportunity Employer Return to All Job Openings 1000 Edgewood College Dr, Madison, WI 53711 Contact Us About Academics Tuition & Financial Aid Student Life Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Edgewood News Store Employment Directory Resources for: Current Students Parents and Families Edgewood Alumni Veterans Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube © 2026 Edgewood University. All rights reserved. Federal Compliance Non-Discriminatory Policy Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://www.edgewood.edu/employment/social-media-strategist/": {
      "title": "Social Media Strategist",
      "description": "Social Media Strategist - Edgewood University Skip to content Menu Search Search Search Button About More About About Accreditation Leadership Board of Trustees Maps & Directions History Fast Facts Mission, Values, and Inclusion Events This is Edgewood Fast Facts Explore quick facts about our college, academics, student body, and more. View Fast Facts Events Check out what's happening on campus, including fine arts, theatre, music, alumni events, and all student events. See All Events Academics More Academics Academics Academic Calendar Online Learning Institutional Review Board Academic Catalog Academic Support Global Education Honors Program Library Partner Schools Pre-Health Professional Pathways Academic Colleges Programs Discover our 80+ undergraduate and graduate academic programs. Explore All Programs Request a Transcript Request an official copy of your academic records. Request Your Transcript Admissions More Admissions Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Transfer Student Admissions International Undergraduate Admissions Military and Veterans Admissions How to Apply View admissions requirements and get ready to apply to Edgewood University View How to Apply Tuition & Financial Aid More Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Payment Options Scholarships Looking for aid that you don't need to pay back? Check out our scholarships. Jump to Scholarships Student Life More Student Life Student Life Housing Dining Orientation Wellness Center Title IX Disability and Accessibility Services Career Development Cutting Edge Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Campus Ministry Living in Madison Housing Come see where you'll live, learn and make friends on campus. Explore Housing Parking and Safety Get an escort, ride the shuttle service, report a security or safety concern, or get a parking permit. Access Services Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Open Search Information Quick Links. Resources for Current Students Parents and Families Alumni Veterans Community Social Media Strategist Home / Employment / Social Media Strategist DESCRIPTION OF JOB: Edgewood University’s Office of Marketing and Strategic Communications (MSC) is seeking a motivated, resourceful, and tech-savvy individual to serve as Social Media Strategist. The Strategist will work directly with the MSC team to strategize and create original content for social media platforms and analyze target audience engagement. The individual will partner with faculty, staff, students, and alumni to create content that is within the Edgewood brand, generates awareness on social media channels, establish goals for programmatic and admissions content/engagement, within Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, and LinkedIn. he individual will partner with faculty, staff, students, and alumni to create content that is within the Edgewood brand, generates awareness on social media channels, establish goals for programmatic and admissions content/engagement, within Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, and LinkedIn. Additionally, this person will provide training, education, and support about social media best practices, planning, brand voice/tone, and strategy. This position will assist with other digital and multimedia projects assigned. Reporting to the AVP for Marketing Strategy, the Social Media Strategist is a full-time, in-person, position. While this position typically works 8:00 a.m.-4:30 p.m. Monday through Friday, occasional weekend and evening hours will be required. We are seeking someone who is: An innovative thinker An independent worker Resourceful and takes initiative Able to thrive in a busy and deadline-driven environment Flexible and adaptable Exciting to multi-task Responsibilities: The Social Media Strategist will be primarily responsible for strengthening and bringing greater visibility to the Edgewood University brand by: Research, brainstorm, and strategize engaging social media content to capture target audiences, including prospective families, alumni, current students and parents, and community members. Content specific to social media channels includes: Generate, edit, and publish scheduled content that aligns with strategic goals for engagement and awareness for the University’s external audiences. Channels include: Facebook, Instagram, and LinkedIn Create innovative and original written content for social media accounts; Produce photographic and video content for social media accounts; Maintain and optimize the social media content calendar to ensure consistent, strategic postings; Collaborate with Graphic Designer to create social media graphics; Track and report on the University’s social media analytics on a quarterly basis. Ensure the University’s brand identity, voice, tone, style is consistent to branding guidelines and across all platforms. Create a vibrant content strategy that will increase awareness, engagement, and inquiries Grow social media presence by maintaining social media profiles with new content 3-4 times each week; Stay up to date with current trends and new tools to increase engagement; Seek out stories and non-athletic events to promote through social media channels; Attend in person events to produce content for social media (may include opportunities for video or photo); Use insights and results of A/B testing to guide content strategy; Elevate the Edgewood University brand ensuring brand identity, voice, tone, and style is consistent to branding guidelines. Provide annual training, education, and support about social media best practices, planning, brand voice/tone, and strategy for both internal partners/areas and external partners. Review, monitor, and respond to comments on organic and paid social media posts and ads that maintain the Edgewood University brand tone and voice. Analyze and interpret data from social media analytics Measure and report performance of social media campaigns and assess against goals. Create reports for review by the marketing, advancement, and admissions team. Monitor competition and provide suggestions for improvement. Capture photos and videos, which would require attendance at campus events, athletics competitions, graduation, etc. Other duties as assigned JOB QUALIFICATIONS Necessary Education or Work Experience: Bachelor’s degree in marketing, communications, journalism, business or a related field Minimum of 1 years marketing and/or communications or social media experience preferred Required Knowledge and Skills: Demonstrated ability to write, create a content plan, manage, and assess multiple social media channels Excellent interpersonal and oral communication skills Understand KPI’s and define specifically for social media Strong functional knowledge of social media principles, practices, and the ability to execute knowledge in a professional environment Demonstrated creativity and ability to handle multiple projects while meeting concurrent deadlines Ability to establish and maintain strong and collaborative working relationships with key constituencies An understanding and interest in strategic marketing communications, storytelling, and enhancing the student experience through meaningful, social connections Specialized Technology Skills: Experience with the Microsoft Office suite Experience with video editing software and social media platforms Other Qualifications: Edgewood University, a Catholic university sponsored by the Dominican Sisters of Sinsinawa, is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to academic excellence through diversity in its faculty, staff, and students. Candidates must demonstrate multicultural competence – the awareness, knowledge, and skills needed to work with others who are culturally different from self in meaningful, relevant, and productive ways. Applicants from traditionally underrepresented populations including women and racial and ethnic minorities are especially encouraged to apply. The selected candidate must actively support the mission of the University by working with faculty, staff and students to share in our core values – truth, compassion, justice, partnership, and community. Must be authorized to work lawfully in the United States without Employer Sponsorship. How to Apply Send one PDF document which includes cover letter, resume, and references with a subject line that includes the position code SCMC : Edgewood University Human Resources – SCMC 1000 Edgewood College Drive Madison, WI 53711 E-mail: humanresources@edgewood.edu Equal Opportunity Employer Return to All Job Openings 1000 Edgewood College Dr, Madison, WI 53711 Contact Us About Academics Tuition & Financial Aid Student Life Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Edgewood News Store Employment Directory Resources for: Current Students Parents and Families Edgewood Alumni Veterans Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube © 2026 Edgewood University. All rights reserved. Federal Compliance Non-Discriminatory Policy Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://www.edgewood.edu/employment/technology-support-specialist/": {
      "title": "Technology Support Specialist",
      "description": "Technology Support Specialist - Edgewood University Skip to content Menu Search Search Search Button About More About About Accreditation Leadership Board of Trustees Maps & Directions History Fast Facts Mission, Values, and Inclusion Events This is Edgewood Fast Facts Explore quick facts about our college, academics, student body, and more. View Fast Facts Events Check out what's happening on campus, including fine arts, theatre, music, alumni events, and all student events. See All Events Academics More Academics Academics Academic Calendar Online Learning Institutional Review Board Academic Catalog Academic Support Global Education Honors Program Library Partner Schools Pre-Health Professional Pathways Academic Colleges Programs Discover our 80+ undergraduate and graduate academic programs. Explore All Programs Request a Transcript Request an official copy of your academic records. Request Your Transcript Admissions More Admissions Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Transfer Student Admissions International Undergraduate Admissions Military and Veterans Admissions How to Apply View admissions requirements and get ready to apply to Edgewood University View How to Apply Tuition & Financial Aid More Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Payment Options Scholarships Looking for aid that you don't need to pay back? Check out our scholarships. Jump to Scholarships Student Life More Student Life Student Life Housing Dining Orientation Wellness Center Title IX Disability and Accessibility Services Career Development Cutting Edge Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Campus Ministry Living in Madison Housing Come see where you'll live, learn and make friends on campus. Explore Housing Parking and Safety Get an escort, ride the shuttle service, report a security or safety concern, or get a parking permit. Access Services Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Open Search Information Quick Links. Resources for Current Students Parents and Families Alumni Veterans Community Technology Support Specialist Home / Employment / Technology Support Specialist DESCRIPTION OF JOB: The Technology Support Specialist provides high-quality and timely technical support for end user computer systems, software, instructional technology and related peripheral equipment in use at Edgewood University Use ‘Best Practice” methods as defined by internal knowledge base articles, university policies, and industry standards in pursuit of the support of our academic technology environment. Responsibilities: Customer service skills, to include face-to-face, audio and text communications. Support and maintain desktop computing, instructional technology equipment and related hardware and software on Edgewood University campus(s). Technical support for multi-media, Special Event related activities as required by the Information Technology Services Office. Basic technical support for telephone and swipe card security equipment. Must be able to work evenings and weekends on as needed basis as required by Special Event technology support assigned by the Service Desk Manager. Assist in set up and implementation of new technology on campus. Aid in the training of Faculty and Staff concerning hardware and software available. Provide Faculty and Staff with technical support to resolve questions and problems. Work with leadership in the documentation of procedures. Comply with software licensing practices for all areas of the university. Help coordinate office staff and work-study Students in support of our computer help desk and computer labs and classrooms as requested by the Supervisors of the Office. Must be able to work non-standard hours on a regularly scheduled basis as set forth by the area Supervisor. Provide orientation for students or staff when requested by Supervisor. Assist the senior office staff and its management as requested. ADDITIONAL JOB FUNCTIONS (training provided) Knowledge and operation of service desk software and procedures. Knowledge and operation of check-out module and procedures. Knowledge and operation of AV production technology and procedures. Ability to monitor, train, and assist work-study students in the overall requirements of Technology Assistance Center operation. Complete competence in all other duties required as first contact: Ability to efficiently diagnose and troubleshoot issues involving but not limited to: Office technology, including desktop computers and peripherals. Printer and copier usage and problems. Desktop software usage and problems. Level 1 infrastructure connectivity. Heartland 1Card technology limited to swipes and cards. Competency in PC software and hardware installation, including peripherals. Familiarity with campus technology and requirements. Basic knowledge of network file sharing and software architecture. Basic knowledge of TCP-IP switch and server architecture on campus. JOB QUALIFICATIONS Necessary Education or Work Experience: Two-year degree in Information Technology Systems or related professional experience. Must be able to work independently with minimum supervision with the ability to coordinate with individuals from other departments to accomplish required tasks and objectives. Required Knowledge and Skills: Overall Proficient skill-level in Microsoft Office, which includes: Word, Excel, Power Point, Outlook, and basic computer concepts. Willingness and ability to learn new software Multicultural Competence – the awareness, knowledge, and skills needed to work with others who are culturally different from self in meaningful, relevant, and productive ways. Good learning, creative and conceptual skills in order to assist users in supporting “Best Practice” use of technology. Pleasant personality and ability to relate to many types of people. Ability to learn independently and grow in a dynamically changing environment. Familiarity with current core technologies in use at Edgewood University: Microsoft Office applications. Microsoft Windows desktop operating system. Adobe family of graphics and multi-media software. MacOS operating systems. Network printing technologies General IP networking technologies. General computer hardware technologies. General analog and digital audio and video multi-media technologies. General telephone equipment & technologies. Other Qualifications: Edgewood University, a Catholic university sponsored by the Dominican Sisters of Sinsinawa, is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to academic excellence through diversity in its faculty, staff, and students. Candidates must demonstrate multicultural competence – the awareness, knowledge, and skills needed to work with others who are culturally different from self in meaningful, relevant, and productive ways. Applicants from traditionally underrepresented populations including women and racial and ethnic minorities are especially encouraged to apply. The selected candidate must actively support the mission of the University by working with faculty, staff and students to share in our core values – truth, compassion, justice, partnership, and community. Must be authorized to work lawfully in the United States without Employer Sponsorship. First consideration will be given to application materials received by January 30, 2026. How to Apply Send one PDF document which includes cover letter, resume, and references with a subject line that includes the position code TESS : Edgewood University Human Resources – TESS 1000 Edgewood College Drive Madison, WI 53711 E-mail: humanresources@edgewood.edu Equal Opportunity Employer Return to All Job Openings 1000 Edgewood College Dr, Madison, WI 53711 Contact Us About Academics Tuition & Financial Aid Student Life Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Edgewood News Store Employment Directory Resources for: Current Students Parents and Families Edgewood Alumni Veterans Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube © 2026 Edgewood University. All rights reserved. Federal Compliance Non-Discriminatory Policy Privacy Statement"
    },
    "https://www.edgewood.edu/employment/undergraduate-admissions-counselor/": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Undergraduate Admissions Counselor - Edgewood University Skip to content Menu Search Search Search Button About More About About Accreditation Leadership Board of Trustees Maps & Directions History Fast Facts Mission, Values, and Inclusion Events This is Edgewood Fast Facts Explore quick facts about our college, academics, student body, and more. View Fast Facts Events Check out what's happening on campus, including fine arts, theatre, music, alumni events, and all student events. See All Events Academics More Academics Academics Academic Calendar Online Learning Institutional Review Board Academic Catalog Academic Support Global Education Honors Program Library Partner Schools Pre-Health Professional Pathways Academic Colleges Programs Discover our 80+ undergraduate and graduate academic programs. Explore All Programs Request a Transcript Request an official copy of your academic records. Request Your Transcript Admissions More Admissions Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Transfer Student Admissions International Undergraduate Admissions Military and Veterans Admissions How to Apply View admissions requirements and get ready to apply to Edgewood University View How to Apply Tuition & Financial Aid More Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Payment Options Scholarships Looking for aid that you don't need to pay back? Check out our scholarships. Jump to Scholarships Student Life More Student Life Student Life Housing Dining Orientation Wellness Center Title IX Disability and Accessibility Services Career Development Cutting Edge Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Campus Ministry Living in Madison Housing Come see where you'll live, learn and make friends on campus. Explore Housing Parking and Safety Get an escort, ride the shuttle service, report a security or safety concern, or get a parking permit. Access Services Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Open Search Information Quick Links. Resources for Current Students Parents and Families Alumni Veterans Community Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Home / Employment / Undergraduate Admissions Counselor DESCRIPTION OF JOB: Edgewood University is seeking a full-time Undergraduate Admissions Counselor. The Admissions Counselor will join our team of admissions professionals dedicated to recruiting, admitting, and enrolling the next generation of Edgewood University undergraduates. The Admissions Counselor will guide students and families through the admissions process from start to finish. The counselor is expected to be knowledgeable across student populations but will predominantly serve new entering first-year undergraduate students and their families. The counselor will develop, manage and implement a recruitment plan for students to include school/site visits, college/career fairs, stakeholder contacts, campus visits, and all follow-up through enrollment. The counselor will also be responsible for reporting progress towards recruitment goals; assisting in the planning and implementation of special events, as well as communicating with prospective students outside of normal office hours. Responsibilities: Admissions Counseling/Advising Prospective Students and Outreach Promote Edgewood University and illustrate our strategic advantage in the marketplace. Counsel prospective students and their families on the admissions process, and financial aid by phone, email, and in person. Represent the Admissions Office at on-campus and off-campus events and programming for prospective students. Travel will be required to high schools and various college fairs. Research national, regional, state, and institutional trends and execute a recruitment plan for attracting, recruiting, and enrolling new entering first year students. Evaluate recruitment strategies and manage student outreach and communication for an assigned territory or special student population. Review admission applications and evaluate credential to make admissions decisions. Complete routine reports related to recruitment goals and enrollment projections. Assist in designing & creating partnerships with pre-college programs such as AVID/TOPS, Early College Credit Programming. Travel Create a Fall Travel & Spring schedule to top feeder high schools & fairs in efforts to increase applications and interest of perspective students Establish working relationships with High School guidance counselors about upcoming visit opportunities & evening fairs Attend between 8-10 recruitment fairs throughout recruiting cycle, throughout personal recruitment territory Must have valid driver’s license and pass Edgewood University Drive Safety protocols Coordination of Campus Events and Programming Assist in the coordination and development of on-campus events for prospective students. Please note, events may take place during non-traditional working hours such as nights & weekends. Assist in designing new programs that attract prospective students. JOB QUALIFICATIONS Necessary Education or Work Experience: Bachelor’s degree required. Minimum of 1 year of relevant work experience in Admissions, Sales, Advising, Education, Student Affairs, Business Development, Customer Service, or experience through course work in Business, Communications, or Marketing. Required Knowledge and Skills: Ability to work independently and contribute as a member of the admissions team. Self-directed in developing and completing projects, recruitment plans, etc. Ability to work fluctuating and irregular hours including nights and weekends. Must be willing to travel 80% of the time during peak travel seasons. Possess a valid Wisconsin driver’s license and be able to drive a University-owned vehicle for high school visits and college fairs. The incumbent must successfully complete a Motor Vehicle Check. Preference for a bilingual candidate with the ability to write and speak in Spanish proficiently. Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to speak in public to large and small groups. Specialized Technology Skills: Knowledge and experience with a student information database and/or Customer Relationship Management software. Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite Preference for experience with Slate CRM. Other Qualifications: Edgewood University, a Catholic university sponsored by the Dominican Sisters of Sinsinawa, is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to academic excellence through diversity in its faculty, staff, and students. Candidates must demonstrate multicultural competence – the awareness, knowledge, and skills needed to work with others who are culturally different from self in meaningful, relevant, and productive ways. Applicants from traditionally underrepresented populations including women and racial and ethnic minorities are especially encouraged to apply. The selected candidate must actively support the mission of the University by working with faculty, staff and students to share in our core values – truth, compassion, justice, partnership, and community. Must be authorized to work lawfully in the United States without Employer Sponsorship. How to Apply Send one PDF document which includes cover letter, resume, and references with a subject line that includes the position code FADC : Edgewood University Human Resources – FADC 1000 Edgewood College Drive Madison, WI 53711 E-mail: humanresources@edgewood.edu Equal Opportunity Employer Return to All Job Openings 1000 Edgewood College Dr, Madison, WI 53711 Contact Us About Academics Tuition & Financial Aid Student Life Athletics MyEC Apply Request Information Visit Give Edgewood News Store Employment Directory Resources for: Current Students Parents and Families Edgewood Alumni Veterans Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube © 2026 Edgewood University. All rights reserved. Federal Compliance Non-Discriminatory Policy Privacy Statement"
    }
